/target
# check-macos.ps1 keeps its own, because sharing one with the Windows build makes every
# switch between the two targets rebuild everything.
/target-macos
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Calibration output (AUTOMATION_PLATFORM_CALIBRATE=1): local measuring aids.
modules/*/calibration/

# Packaged builds — `package.ps1` output. The staged tree is 58 MB of binaries and the zip
# another 28; both are reproducible from a tag and neither belongs in the history.
dist/

# Agent worktrees created by background tasks — separate checkouts, not content.
/.claude/

# Test data that must never be committed: a frame of a commercial game, and the reference
# vectors an outside reader computed from it, for the `host.screen.cells` golden test
# (crates/host/src/cells_golden_tests.rs). The test skips, saying why, when the folder is
# missing; the region numbers it also checks are in region.rs, where they may live.
crates/host/tests-data-local/

# Probe output: a window capture plus its dump, written next to the tool that made it.
# Evidence for one measurement, not something to carry in the history — and deleting it by
# hand once cost the measurement it was taken for.
probe-*.png
voiceover.sdef

# Test protocols and the tester briefing: working papers for ONE session with one tester —
# which keys to press, in which order, on a machine nobody here owns. They change for every
# session, they are sent to one person by hand, and on the documentation site they would read
# as instructions to whoever finds them. The design and reference pages beside them stay.
docs/macos-session-*.md
docs/macos-tester-briefing.md
docs/macos-test-protocol*.md
